                            <comment id="16722922" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 17 Dec 2018 12:04:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user aealeksandrov opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/5682&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/5682&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-10716&quot; title=&quot;Rest clients should call ctx.security().onSessionExpired(subjid) on disconnect to avoid the possible leaking of the memory&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-10716&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-10716&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: ctx.security().onSessionExpired(subjid) is called on re&#8230;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &#8230;st session expiration now.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    At the moment ctx.security().onSessionExpired(subjid) didn&apos;t called on rest session expiration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    It provides the leaking of the memory related to resources that were generated during authentification&lt;/p&gt;

